    {
      "text": "Gentiles will bring Israel’s sons in their arms, 1 Ne. 21:22 (22:6; 2 Ne. 6:6; Isa. 49:22). Abraham’s offering up his son, Isaac, was similitude of God and his Son, Jacob 4:5. Benjamin declares his son Mosiah2 king, Mosiah 2:30. those who enter covenant are called sons and daughters of Christ, Mosiah 5:7. those born again of God become his sons and daughters, Mosiah 27:25. Lamanites believe Nephites are sons of liar, Alma 20:13. the 2,000 sons of Ammonites have taken up weapons of war, Alma 56:3, 5. land north called Mulek after son of Zedekiah1, Hel. 6:10. sons of Zedekiah1 were slain, except Mulek, Hel. 8:21. what man, if son ask bread, will give him stone, 3 Ne. 14:9 (Matt. 7:9). those who believe on Christ’s name become his sons and daughters, Ether 3:14.",
